  "_definition": "Each entry records the reporting requirement at a CVFR waypoint per the IAA chart's 'סוג דיווח' column: 'mandatory' (חובה) — pilots must report on overflight; 'on-request' (דרישה) — pilots report only when ATC asks; 'arp' (ARP / Aerodrome Reference Point) — listed for reference but not itself a reporting fix. Distinct from 'commChange' (docs/comm-change.json), which marks points where pilots are expected to change ATC frequencies.",
  "_TODO": [
    "Cross-reference with nav-waypoints.json: 9 non-ARP transcript codes do not exist in nav-waypoints.json. Two are pure code-mismatches for the same point (the chart and ForeFlight Israel Base Pack disagree on the 5-letter code): NASIH (אשל הנשיא, mandatory) ≡ nav-waypoints ESHEL (אשל-הנשיא); ZGOAL (גורל, mandatory) ≡ nav-waypoints GORAL (גורל). Resolve by either renaming the nav-waypoints entry to match the chart, adding an aliases field, or keeping both spellings discoverable. Decide separately from this dataset.",
    "Seven additional non-ARP transcript codes are absent from nav-waypoints.json entirely; record their lat/lng from the chart and decide whether to add them to nav-waypoints.json as a follow-up: LLMZ (מצדה, mandatory — also LL-prefixed yet listed mandatory not ARP, possibly Masada strip used as a reporting point), MESEK (משק, mandatory), METAH (מתח, mandatory), ZURIM (עין צורים, mandatory — distinct from ZUKIM עינות-צוקים), TZHOT (צלחות, on-request), ZRANA (רעננה מרכז, mandatory), RANNO (רעננה צפון, mandatory).",
    "Duplicate code in source: LLNV appears twice in the chart table — once as נבטים (Nevatim) and once as נגב (Negev). The dataset stores one entry under LLNV (parser keeps the first occurrence, נבטים). Confirm with chart authors whether this is two co-located airfields sharing a code or a chart layout artefact.",
